## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/config_save_merge.dart | ⚠️ important global scope edits are persisted into the repo traveling project file the targeting criterion in projecttargets is the section changed vs the baseline and the project file carries the section — it never asks which scope the edit belongs to persistconfig s overlays are global scope values bin fah runapp dart 2093 2097 passes tools cli globaltools the global view and ontoolsconfigchanged is documented as the user changes the global tools scope … so the executable can persist the cli s live global view globaltools lib src cli agent cli config dart 552 554 reproduced live writable workspace project file seeded with tools web search false after the tools enable web search global equivalent save project file now web search true global file keeps web search false a subsequent unrelated mode architect persist leaves the global file at web search false — the toggle never reaches the global file on this or any other machine the block is shadowed never re rendered by design and the repo traveling file now carries a machine local toggle that travels via git this contradicts the repl s own scope model — tools exposes separate global and project scopes and mergetoolsintofile merges per key surgically when the user picks project it also re fires on every later persist the live overlay never returns to the boot baseline and saved never learns about project writes each mode model provider approval switch rewrites the project file content identical rename → mtime churn on a possibly git tracked file the help text s the scope that wins at boot rationale is loose for tools specifically — its project scope is consumed live and stacked per key lib src cli cli config dart 1070 1072 so a global toggle for a key the project does not name would take effect from the global file without any targeting suggested direction target only sections whose change cannot take effect from the global file boot precedence genuinely shadowed e g the cube startup default or make the targeting scope aware per key for tools mirror mergetoolsintofile or exclude global scope overlays from targeting for the persistconfig caller global exists as an escape hatch but the user gets no signal that their global toggle landed in a repo file |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/config_save_merge.dart | ⚠️ important an unwritable workspace fah dir turns every later persistconfig into a raw throw savechangedprojectsections degrades gracefully for an unparseable project file parseyamlmapornull → target nothing documented but an unwritable one throws the atomic write tmp writeasstring rename fails with a raw pathaccessexception that propagates out of savecliconfig and out of the persistconfig hooks reproduced live chmod 555 on project fah threw pathaccessexception cannot open file path … proj fah config yaml tmp 7426 0 os error permission denied errno 13 pre pr tools id global cube picks mode model provider … all wrote only the user home and succeeded in exactly the workspace this pr s own global doc describes workspaces whose project file is not this machine s to edit post pr they hard fail there and because a targeted section stays baseline for the process lifetime the hook never re syncs saved for project writes every subsequent persistconfig throws until restart — one toggle bricks config persistence for the session the boot save only catches configexception bin fah runapp dart 2120 2126 so an fs error would surface as an unhandled error and the sibling tools project write deliberately prints and returns false for the same condition lib src cli agent cli tools dart 920 924 suggested direction treat an unwritable project destination like the unparseable one — degrade to the global destination with a warning line consistent with mergetoolsintofile s contract or catch fs errors at the hook boundary no test currently pins this failure contract |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | lib/src/cli/config_save_merge.dart | 💡 suggestion project targets are computed outside the write chain — same section lost update projecttargets runs against a snapshot read before serializedconfigwrite file path … acquires the chain line 188 reads the doc line 190 enters the chain inside the chain the text is re read but the precomputed targets and newblocks are applied verbatim — so another process s write to the same section that lands between the snapshot and the chain acquisition is clobbered section granularity lost update the global path handles this correctly it re reads disktext inside the chain and merges mergewithondisk there which is exactly the discipline gh 2422 is about suggest recomputing the targets or at least re checking sectionchanged against the freshly read text inside the chain callback narrow window two writers same section near simultaneous hence a suggestion rather than a blocker — but it is the one place in this pr where the serialization the save machinery advertises is not actually load bearing |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

